Subject: [PATCH 0/3] Bluetooth: btusb: Fix deferred URB leaks and races

btusb defers a transmit URB while the device is suspending or
suspended, anchors it on data->deferred, and sends it at the next
resume. Three things can go wrong with such a URB:

 1: when it is discarded instead of sent (btusb_close(), a failed
    resume, or a failed submission in play_deferred()), the skb it
    carries is never freed, and at two of the four places neither is
    its setup packet;
 2: submit_or_queue_tx_urb() anchors it after dropping txlock, so a
    resume that completes in between leaves it anchored on an active
    device until the next suspend and resume;
 3: a failed resume drops the deferred URBs before it clears
    BTUSB_SUSPENDING under txlock, so a URB anchored in between is
    left behind in the same way.

An HCI command left behind as in 2 or 3 times out. Patch 3 relies on
patch 2. Patch 1 is independent of both and comes first, so that it
can be taken alone.

Tested in QEMU guests with KASAN, lockdep, kmemleak and hung-task
detection, four CPUs, with an emulated QCA9377 (13d3:3503) attached
over usbip to btusb. Fault injection and delays were in the test kernel
only. Each patch's notes give its case. Beyond those, six other
emulated cases (a dead device, a device that answers after the
reset-resume, a dropped event with and without a wedged controller, 30
suspend and resume cycles, power-off during a resume) and a 100-cycle
stress run with concurrent senders gave the same results on the base
tree and with the series, apart from the leaks it removes. The
power-off case fails on both and is not addressed here. There were no
kernel reports in any run.

Iaroslav Voitovych (3):
  Bluetooth: btusb: Free the skb of a deferred URB that is discarded
  Bluetooth: btusb: Anchor a deferred URB under txlock
  Bluetooth: btusb: Drop deferred URBs under txlock on a failed resume

